@page "/theory"

<PageTitle>Mathematical Foundations - EOH 2026</PageTitle>

<div class="container mt-4 mb-5">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-lg-9 mx-auto">
            <h1 class="display-4 mb-4 pb-2" style="font-family: var(--eoh-font-headings); font-weight: 300; letter-spacing: -0.05rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--eoh-border);">Mathematical Foundations</h1>

            <p class="lead text-muted fst-italic" style="font-family: var(--eoh-font-serif); font-size: 1.3rem; line-height: 1.7; border-left: 3px solid var(--eoh-altgeld-orange); padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
                A formal treatment of the partitioning logic and statistical resolution engine employed by the EOH 2026 Relative Judging System.
            </p>

            <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--eoh-orange);">
                <div class="card-body p-4 p-md-5">
                    <h2 class="h3 mb-3" style="font-family: var(--eoh-font-headings); font-weight: 600; color: var(--eoh-blue);">
                        <span class="badge me-2 px-2 py-1" style="background-color: var(--eoh-orange); color: white; font-size: 0.85rem;">I</span>
                        The Problem of Sparse Comparisons
                    </h2>

                    <div class="row align-items-start">
                        <div class="col-lg-7 order-2 order-lg-1">
                            <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--eoh-charcoal); line-height: 1.75;">
                                In a traditional contest with $N$ entries, a total ordering requires $\binom{N}{2}$ pairwise comparisons. As $N$ grows, the workload becomes $O(N^2)$, which is infeasible for human judges. To mitigate this, we employ <strong>Partitioned Judging</strong>. We divide the population into $k$ subsets, but this introduces a new risk: <em>disjoint graphs</em>. Without overlapping data, it is mathematically impossible to compare an entry in Group A with an entry in Group B.
                            </p>
                            <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--eoh-charcoal); line-height: 1.75;">
                                We resolve this by designating $B$ entries as <strong>Bridge Nodes</strong>. These nodes appear in <em>every</em> partition, acting as common baselines that allow us to project local ranks onto a global manifold.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-lg-5 order-1 order-lg-2 mb-4 mb-lg-0">
                            <svg viewBox="0 0 320 240" style="width: 100%; max-width: 320px; display: block; margin: 0 auto;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                                <defs>
                                    <filter id="shadow1" x="-10%" y="-10%" width="120%" height="120%">
                                        <feDropShadow dx="0" dy="2" stdDeviation="3" style="flood-color: var(--eoh-charcoal); flood-opacity: 0.08"/>
                                    </filter>
                                </defs>
                                <!-- Partition 0 -->
                                <rect x="12" y="20" width="170" height="100" rx="14" style="fill: var(--eoh-azure); opacity: 0.08; stroke: var(--eoh-azure)" stroke-width="1.2" filter="url(#shadow1)"/>
                                <text x="60" y="36" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="9" style="fill: var(--eoh-azure)" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Group 0</text>
                                <!-- Partition 1 -->
                                <rect x="138" y="18" width="170" height="100" rx="14" style="fill: var(--eoh-warm-neutral); opacity: 0.6; stroke: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange)" stroke-width="1.2" filter="url(#shadow1)"/>
                                <text x="200" y="34" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="9" style="fill: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange)" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Group 1</text>
                                <!-- Partition 2 -->
                                <rect x="75" y="110" width="170" height="100" rx="14" style="fill: var(--eoh-light-gray); stroke: var(--eoh-purple)" stroke-width="1.2" filter="url(#shadow1)"/>
                                <text x="160" y="126" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="9" style="fill: var(--eoh-purple)" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Group 2</text>

                                <!-- Bridge nodes (orange) - appear in all 3 groups -->
                                <circle cx="160" cy="55" r="8" style="fill: var(--eoh-orange); opacity: 0.85"/>
                                <circle cx="160" cy="55" r="3.5" fill="white"/>
                                <text x="160" y="47" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="8" style="fill: var(--eoh-orange)" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">B₁</text>

                                <circle cx="190" cy="85" r="8" style="fill: var(--eoh-orange); opacity: 0.85"/>
                                <circle cx="190" cy="85" r="3.5" fill="white"/>
                                <text x="190" y="77" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="8" style="fill: var(--eoh-orange)" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">B₂</text>

                                <!-- Partition 0 unique nodes (blue) -->
                                <circle cx="45" cy="52" r="7" style="fill: var(--eoh-blue); opacity: 0.6"/>
                                <circle cx="80" cy="90" r="7" style="fill: var(--eoh-blue); opacity: 0.6"/>
                                <circle cx="110" cy="48" r="7" style="fill: var(--eoh-blue); opacity: 0.6"/>

                                <!-- Partition 1 unique nodes (blue) -->
                                <circle cx="235" cy="50" r="7" style="fill: var(--eoh-blue); opacity: 0.6"/>
                                <circle cx="270" cy="85" r="7" style="fill: var(--eoh-blue); opacity: 0.6"/>

                                <!-- Partition 2 unique nodes (blue) -->
                                <circle cx="115" cy="160" r="7" style="fill: var(--eoh-blue); opacity: 0.6"/>
                                <circle cx="180" cy="180" r="7" style="fill: var(--eoh-blue); opacity: 0.6"/>

                                <!-- Legend -->
                                <circle cx="245" cy="170" r="5" style="fill: var(--eoh-orange); opacity: 0.85"/><circle cx="245" cy="170" r="2" fill="white"/>
                                <text x="255" y="173" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="9" style="fill: var(--eoh-charcoal)">Bridge node</text>
                                <circle cx="245" cy="190" r="5" style="fill: var(--eoh-blue); opacity: 0.6"/>
                                <text x="255" y="193" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="9" style="fill: var(--eoh-charcoal)">Unique node</text>
                            </svg>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--eoh-altgeld-orange);">
                <div class="card-body p-4 p-md-5">
                    <h2 class="h3 mb-4" style="font-family: var(--eoh-font-headings); font-weight: 600; color: var(--eoh-blue);">
                        <span class="badge me-2 px-2 py-1" style="background-color: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange); color: white; font-size: 0.85rem;">II</span>
                        The Bradley-Terry Model
                    </h2>
                    <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75;">
                        Once the relational data is collected, we treat the results not as a fixed hierarchy, but as a set of probabilistic outcomes. We assume each entry $i$ has an underlying "strength" $\gamma_i > 0$. The probability that entry $i$ is judged superior to entry $j$ is given by the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bradley%E2%80%93Terry_model" target="_blank" style="color: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange); font-weight: 600;">Bradley-Terry Model</a><sup>1</sup>:
                    </p>

                    <div class="row g-4 my-4 align-items-center">
                        <div class="col-lg-6">
                            <div class="p-4 bg-light">
                                <p class="text-center text-muted small mb-0" style="font-family: var(--eoh-font-headings); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05rem; font-size: 0.75rem;">Winning Probability</p>
                                <h4 class="fw-bold mb-0 text-center" style="color: var(--eoh-blue);">$$P(i > j) = \frac{\gamma_i}{\gamma_i + \gamma_j}$$</h4>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-lg-6">
                            <svg viewBox="0 0 340 230" style="width: 100%; max-width: 340px; display: block; margin: 0 auto;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                                <defs>
                                    <linearGradient id="curveGrad" x1="0%" y1="100%" x2="100%" y2="0%">
                                        <stop offset="0%" style="stop-color: var(--eoh-blue); stop-opacity: 0.15"/>
                                        <stop offset="100%" style="stop-color: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange); stop-opacity: 0.15"/>
                                    </linearGradient>
                                </defs>
                                <!-- Horizontal grid lines at P=0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0 -->
                                <line x1="50" y1="200" x2="310" y2="200" style="stroke: var(--eoh-border)" stroke-width="0.5"/>
                                <line x1="50" y1="163" x2="310" y2="163" style="stroke: var(--eoh-border)" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>
                                <line x1="50" y1="125" x2="310" y2="125" style="stroke: var(--eoh-border)" stroke-width="0.5"/>
                                <line x1="50" y1="88" x2="310" y2="88" style="stroke: var(--eoh-border)" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>
                                <line x1="50" y1="50" x2="310" y2="50" style="stroke: var(--eoh-border)" stroke-width="0.5"/>

                                <!-- Area under curve: P = x/(x+1), x=0..5 -->
                                <path d="M50,200 L55.2,186.4 L60.4,175.0 L65.6,165.4 L70.8,157.1 L76.0,150.0 L81.2,143.8 L86.4,138.2 L91.6,133.3 L96.8,128.9 L102,125.0 L112.4,118.2 L122.8,112.5 L133.2,107.7 L143.6,103.6 L154,100.0 L164.4,96.9 L174.8,94.1 L206,87.5 L258,80.0 L310,75.0 L310,200 L50,200 Z" fill="url(#curveGrad)" opacity="0.4"/>

                                <!-- Curve: P = γ/(γ+1) for γ from 0 to 5 -->
                                <path d="M50,200 L55.2,186.4 L60.4,175.0 L65.6,165.4 L70.8,157.1 L76.0,150.0 L81.2,143.8 L86.4,138.2 L91.6,133.3 L96.8,128.9 L102,125.0 L112.4,118.2 L122.8,112.5 L133.2,107.7 L143.6,103.6 L154,100.0 L164.4,96.9 L174.8,94.1 L206,87.5 L258,80.0 L310,75.0" style="stroke: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange)" stroke-width="2.5" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>

                                <!-- Annotation: 50% point -->
                                <circle cx="102" cy="125" r="4" style="fill: var(--eoh-blue)"/>
                                <line x1="102" y1="125" x2="102" y2="204" style="stroke: var(--eoh-blue)" stroke-width="0.8" stroke-dasharray="3,2"/>
                                <text x="102" y="216" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="9" style="fill: var(--eoh-blue)" text-anchor="middle">γᵢ = γⱼ</text>

                                <!-- Axes -->
                                <line x1="50" y1="200" x2="320" y2="200" style="stroke: var(--eoh-charcoal)" stroke-width="1"/>
                                <line x1="50" y1="200" x2="50" y2="40" style="stroke: var(--eoh-charcoal)" stroke-width="1"/>

                                <!-- Y-axis tick labels -->
                                <text x="42" y="203" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="8" style="fill: var(--eoh-azure)" text-anchor="end">0</text>
                                <text x="42" y="166" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="8" style="fill: var(--eoh-azure)" text-anchor="end">0.25</text>
                                <text x="42" y="128" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="8" style="fill: var(--eoh-azure)" text-anchor="end">0.5</text>
                                <text x="42" y="91" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="8" style="fill: var(--eoh-azure)" text-anchor="end">0.75</text>
                                <text x="42" y="53" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="8" style="fill: var(--eoh-azure)" text-anchor="end">1</text>

                                <!-- Axis labels -->
                                <text x="180" y="200" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="8" style="fill: var(--eoh-charcoal)" text-anchor="middle" dy="16">Strength Ratio &gamma;<tspan font-size="7" dy="3">i</tspan><tspan font-size="7"> / &gamma;</tspan><tspan font-size="7" dy="3">j</tspan><tspan font-size="7" dy="-3"></tspan></text>

                                <text x="20" y="120" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="8" style="fill: var(--eoh-charcoal)" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(-90, 20, 120)">P(i &gt; j)</text>
                            </svg>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75;">
                        To find the most likely values for $\gamma$, we maximize the <strong>Likelihood Function</strong> $L(\gamma)$:
                    </p>
                    <div class="p-4 bg-light my-3">
                        <h4 class="fw-bold mb-0 text-center" style="color: var(--eoh-blue);">$$L(\gamma) = \prod_{i=1}^n \prod_{j=1}^n \left( \frac{\gamma_i}{\gamma_i + \gamma_j} \right)^{w_{ij}}$$</h4>
                    </div>
                    <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.75;">
                        where $w_{ij}$ is the number of times $i$ beat $j$. Since this function is concave, we find the global maximum using an <strong>Iterative Scaling Algorithm</strong><sup>2</sup>.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm mb-4" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--eoh-blue);">
                <div class="card-body p-4 p-md-5">
                    <h2 class="h3 mb-3" style="font-family: var(--eoh-font-headings); font-weight: 600; color: var(--eoh-blue);">
                        <span class="badge me-2 px-2 py-1" style="background-color: var(--eoh-blue); color: white; font-size: 0.85rem;">III</span>
                        Convergence and Normalization
                    </h2>

                    <div class="row align-items-start">
                        <div class="col-lg-6">
                            <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--eoh-charcoal); line-height: 1.75;">
                                The system iteratively updates the strength parameters until the change between iterations falls below a threshold $\epsilon = 10^{-6}$. To ensure numerical stability across different categories, the final vector $\vec{\gamma}$ is normalized such that $\sum \gamma_i = 1$.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-lg-6 mb-3 mb-lg-0">
                            <svg viewBox="0 0 340 230" style="width: 100%; max-width: 340px; display: block; margin: 0 auto;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                                <defs>
                                    <linearGradient id="convergeGrad" x1="0%" y1="100%" x2="100%" y2="100%">
                                        <stop offset="0%" style="stop-color: var(--eoh-blue); stop-opacity: 0.12"/>
                                        <stop offset="100%" style="stop-color: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange); stop-opacity: 0.12"/>
                                    </linearGradient>
                                </defs>
                                <!-- Grid lines -->
                                <line x1="55" y1="195" x2="315" y2="195" style="stroke: var(--eoh-charcoal)" stroke-width="1"/>
                                <line x1="55" y1="35" x2="55" y2="195" style="stroke: var(--eoh-charcoal)" stroke-width="1"/>

                                <!-- Horizontal grid lines at power-of-10 ticks -->
                                <line x1="55" y1="35" x2="315" y2="35" style="stroke: var(--eoh-border)" stroke-width="0.5"/>
                                <line x1="55" y1="71" x2="315" y2="71" style="stroke: var(--eoh-border)" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>
                                <line x1="55" y1="106" x2="315" y2="106" style="stroke: var(--eoh-border)" stroke-width="0.5"/>
                                <line x1="55" y1="142" x2="315" y2="142" style="stroke: var(--eoh-border)" stroke-width="0.5" stroke-dasharray="4,4"/>
                                <line x1="55" y1="177" x2="315" y2="177" style="stroke: var(--eoh-border)" stroke-width="0.5"/>

                                <!-- Y-axis tick labels (log10 of max relative change) -->
                                <text x="48" y="198" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="7" style="fill: var(--eoh-azure)" text-anchor="end">10⁻⁸</text>
                                <text x="48" y="180" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="7" style="fill: var(--eoh-azure)" text-anchor="end">10⁻⁷</text>
                                <text x="48" y="109" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="7" style="fill: var(--eoh-azure)" text-anchor="end">10⁻⁴</text>
                                <text x="48" y="73" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="7" style="fill: var(--eoh-azure)" text-anchor="end">10⁻²</text>
                                <text x="48" y="38" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="7" style="fill: var(--eoh-azure)" text-anchor="end">10⁰</text>

                                <!-- Convergence threshold line (ε = 10⁻⁶) -->
                                <line x1="55" y1="159" x2="315" y2="159" style="stroke: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange)" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-dasharray="6,4"/>
                                <text x="310" y="156" font-family="Georgia, serif" font-size="8" style="fill: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange)" text-anchor="end" font-weight="600">&epsilon; = 10⁻⁶</text>

                                <!-- Area under convergence curve -->
                                <path d="M55,58 L75,70 L95,81 L115,93 L135,105 L155,116 L175,128 L195,139 L215,151 L235,162 L255,174 L275,184 L295,189 L315,190 L315,195 L55,195 Z" fill="url(#convergeGrad)" opacity="0.3"/>

                                <!-- Convergence curve: error = e^(-0.15*t), log10 scale (linear convergence = straight line on log plot) -->
                                <path d="M55,58 L75,70 L95,81 L115,93 L135,105 L155,116 L175,128 L195,139 L215,151 L235,162 L255,174 L275,184 L295,189 L315,190" style="stroke: var(--eoh-blue)" stroke-width="2.5" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>

                                <!-- Point where curve meets threshold (t≈88, crosses 10⁻⁶) -->
                                <circle cx="284" cy="159" r="4" style="fill: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange)"/>
                                <line x1="284" y1="159" x2="284" y2="198" style="stroke: var(--eoh-altgeld-orange)" stroke-width="0.8" stroke-dasharray="2,3"/>

                                <!-- Axis labels -->
                                <text x="185" y="195" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="9" style="fill: var(--eoh-charcoal)" text-anchor="middle" dy="16">Iteration</text>
                                <text x="20" y="115" font-family="Montserrat, sans-serif" font-size="9" style="fill: var(--eoh-charcoal)" text-anchor="middle" transform="rotate(-90, 20, 115)">max |&Delta;|</text>
                            </svg>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <p style="font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--eoh-charcoal); line-height: 1.75;">
                        For the final cardinal score, we operate in the <strong>Log-Strength Space</strong>. The natural logarithm of $\gamma$ provides a linear interval scale where the distance between scores represents a constant ratio of "winning probability," satisfying the requirements for a fair and transitive leaderboard.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <section class="mt-5 border-top pt-4" style="border-top-color: var(--eoh-border) !important;">
                <h5 class="text-muted" style="font-family: var(--eoh-font-headings); text-transform: uppercase; font-size: 0.85rem; letter-spacing: 0.05rem;">References & Further Reading</h5>
                <ol class="small text-muted" style="line-height: 1.6;">
                    <li><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bradley%E2%80%93Terry_model" target="_blank">Wikipedia: Bradley-Terry Model</a></li>
                    <li><a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/MaximumLikelihoodEstimator.html" target="_blank">Wolfram MathWorld: Maximum Likelihood Estimator</a></li>
                    <li>Hunter, D. R. (2004). "MM algorithms for generalized Bradley-Terry models." <em>The Annals of Statistics</em>.</li>
                </ol>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

